  "name": "Cytomegalovirus (CMV) Antibody-IgM",
  "code": "CMV IGM",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>CMV (Cytomegalovirus) test is used to detect antibodies against the cytomegalovirus.&nbsp;<br></p><table><thead><tr><th><div>CMV Test Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>IgG Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for IgG antibodies indicates past exposure to cytomegalovirus. It suggests that the person has been previously infected with CMV and has developed immunity to the virus. Immunity to future CMV infections is usually provided.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>IgM Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>A positive result for IgM antibodies suggests a recent or current CMV infection. It indicates an ongoing or recent infection. Additional testing and clinical assessment are necessary to confirm the diagnosis.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Both IgG and IgM Antibodies Positive</div></td><td><div>Simultaneous presence of both IgG and IgM antibodies may indicate a recent CMV infection or a reactivation of a previous infection. Further evaluation is required to determine the specific stage and nature of the infection.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Both IgG and IgM Antibodies Negative</div></td><td><div>A negative result for both IgG and IgM antibodies indicates no current or previous exposure to cytomegalovirus and no immunity to the virus. It means the person is susceptible to CMV infection.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
